  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following reversible reaction:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi>AB</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math><br />The activation energy of the backward reaction exceeds that of the forward reaction by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>RT</mi></math>&nbsp;(in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>). If the pre-exponential factor of the forward reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;times that of the reverse reaction, the absolute value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>&#8861;</mo></msup><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>in</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math> for the reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;is ____.<br />(Given; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>.7</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>2500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>at</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math>&nbsp;is the Gibbs energy)"
  },
